; A low ceiling over the middle of the stage, two gaps under it, and a
; hazard hanging from the ceiling's centre. Crossing means going *under* the
; ceiling, where swings are pinned low and the fastest, highest line runs
; into the hazard. Out on the two banks the sky is open, and a short
; staircase of ledges climbs away from the floor.
;
; Rebuilt from scratch for issue #51. The earlier Gauntlet (#18, reworked in
; #45) had 250 px gaps under a ceiling that roofed most of the ground, with
; the ceiling's top as the only high ground. Playtest 2 still found it
; "pretty inaccessible": no pickaxe could reach across a gap, so every
; crossing was a blind fling under the roof, and once the rising lava
; started the only place left to climb was onto the ceiling. The owner kept
; the idea -- a low ceiling, gaps, a hazard in the ceiling, a route under it
; that favours the staff -- and asked that every platform be easy to get on
; and off, and that nothing trap a player. Nobody should have to walk on
; the ceiling to cross (#45).
;
; The reach numbers it is built on. A body is a 24 px circle, so a player
; standing on a surface has its centre 24 px above it, and its head reaches
; max_reach plus a few px of head from that centre: staff 240, pickaxe
; about 159, axe about 151, sword about 124 (the end of its blade), dagger
; about 87. Every weapon but the staff is held to one rule here: each move
; on or off a surface is a hook of 90-110 px, which the pickaxe does easily.
;
;   Ground: every standing surface's top is y=300 (both banks and the
;   middle), so the rising floor takes them together and nobody is left on
;   lower ground than anyone else.
;
;   Gaps: 100 px wide (x=+-190..+-290). A pickaxe at one lip hooks the far
;   lip at about 110 px and hauls itself across; the axe and the sword
;   reach it too. The dagger has to fling, but 100 px is a short hop.
;   Coming back is the same move the other way, so the middle is as easy
;   to leave as it is to reach.
;
;   Ceiling: x=-330..330, underside y=90, 210 px over the ground. It covers
;   the gaps and the middle and overhangs each bank by 40 px, no more. Its
;   underside is 186 px above a standing player's centre: out of reach of
;   the pickaxe and everything shorter, well inside the staff's 240. That
;   is the staff's route: from a bank's lip it plants on the underside out
;   to about x=+-150, swings hand over hand along the ceiling, and crosses
;   both gaps without touching the middle. Everyone else crosses on foot,
;   one hook at a time, under the hazard.
;
;   Hazard: centred under the ceiling, x=-80..80, y=90..138. It leaves
;   114 px of air over a player standing on the middle: room to walk and to
;   swing low, and a kill for anyone swinging or flung upward there. Hung
;   from the ceiling rather than laid on the middle ground, so the ground
;   you land on after a crossing is never itself what kills you.
;
;   Banks: x=+-290..+-660, open sky over everything outboard of the ceiling
;   (|x| > 330). Their outer ends drop straight into the kill zone, so a
;   player hit hard enough outward rings out.
;
;   Low ledges: x=+-620..+-790, top y=190, 110 px up. Their inner 40 px
;   overhang the bank, the rest hangs out over the drop. From the bank just
;   inboard of one, the pickaxe hooks its top corner at about 90 px (the
;   sword too). Off: step off the inner end and you land on the bank.
;
;   High ledges: x=+-400..+-580, top y=80, 110 px above the low ledge and
;   40 px inboard of it. From the low ledge's inner end the pickaxe hooks
;   the high ledge's outer corner at about 108 px; from the bank only the
;   staff reaches it (196 px up). Off: either end drops onto the bank,
;   which runs under the whole ledge.
;
;   The ceiling's top (y=50) is 70 px from a high ledge's inner end and 30
;   px higher, so a pickaxe can hook onto it from there. That is allowed
;   rather than prevented: it is the last high ground once the lava is up,
;   and a wide one to finish a round on, but it is three climbs away and
;   never the way across. Off: either end drops onto a bank.
;
; So nothing traps anyone once the lava rises (grace 50 s, rise 80 s): every
; surface can be left without the staff, and the climb out of the floor --
; bank, low ledge, high ledge, ceiling top -- is a staircase of pickaxe
; hooks with open sky over every step.

; Backdrop (issue #117): cavern.
